## Customization

### Adding Language-Specific Tests

Create new scenario files for specific languages, then list them under `scenarios:` in `config.arena.yaml`:

```yaml
# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://promptkit.altairalabs.ai/schemas/v1alpha1/scenario.json
apiVersion: promptkit.altairalabs.ai/v1alpha1
kind: Scenario
metadata:
  name: javascript-async

spec:
  id: js-async-test
  task_type: code-generation
  description: "Test async/await in JavaScript"
  
  turns:
    - role: user
      content: "Write a JavaScript function that fetches data from an API with error handling"
      assertions:
        - type: contains_any
          params:
            patterns: ["async", "await", "try", "catch"]
```

### Adjusting Code Style

Edit the prompt configurations to enforce specific style guidelines:
- `prompts/code-generator.prompt.yaml` - Generation preferences
- `prompts/code-reviewer.prompt.yaml` - Review criteria

## Running Tests

```bash
# Run all scenarios
promptarena run

# Run specific scenario
promptarena run --scenario code-generation

# Run with specific provider
promptarena run --provider {{range $i, $p := .providers}}{{if eq $i 0}}{{$p}}{{end}}{{end}}

# Test with lower temperature for more deterministic code
promptarena run --temperature 0.1
```

## Results

Test results are saved to `out/`:
- `index.json` and one JSON file per run - Detailed test results
- `results.md` - Markdown report

